Decodium RX - digital-mode receiver for the terminal (receive only)
===================================================================

decodium-rx captures audio from the radio's sound card, cuts it into
UTC-aligned slots (FT8 15 s, FT4 7.5 s, FT2 3.75 s) and decodes each slot
with decodium-rx-core, a command-line build of the Decodium 4 decode
workers: the same C++ decoders the Decodium application runs. It never
transmits and never touches CAT or PTT.

  decodium-rx                       asks mode, dial frequency, callsign and input
  decodium-rx -m ft8 -f 14.074 -c IU8LMC
  decodium-rx -m ft2 -s alsa -d plughw:CARD=CODEC,DEV=0
  decodium-rx --list-devices
  decodium-rx --cq-only             only CQ calls
  decodium-rx --grep 'IU8|JN70'     only matching messages
  rtl_fm -M usb -f 144.174M -s 12k - | decodium-rx -m ft8 -s stdin
  decodium-rx -m ft8 --wav 250913_120000.wav

Decodes are appended to ~/.local/share/decodium-rx/ALL.TXT (WSJT-X
format, --no-log to disable); --save-slots DIR keeps every slot as WAV.
The answers to the start-up questions are remembered in
~/.config/decodium-rx.json.

The system clock must be within about half a second of UTC: DecodiumOS
keeps it synchronised with NTP.

decodium-rx-core is built from the Decodium 4 sources (GPL-3.0,
https://github.com/iu8lmc/Decodium-4.0-Core-Shannon) at the release that
matches the installed Decodium; its version is shown by
  /usr/lib/decodium-rx/decodium-rx-core --version
